# CHIMERE annual-mean air pollution exposure maps

This folder contains annual-mean concentration maps of fine particulate matter (PM2.5) and nitrogen dioxide (NO2) over France, expressed in µg/m³. Maps are provided for a 2019 baseline and for the years 2030 and 2050 under four scenarios (S1 to S4).

The model data were generated by Ineris (Institut national de l'environnement industriel et des risques) using the CHIMERE chemistry-transport model.

Each map is provided as a zip archive containing the full numerical values, in NetCDF format and as a table of coordinates and concentrations, together with a PNG image of the map. A file named manifest.csv lists all files with summary statistics.
